# ============================================================
# .env.example — REFERENCE ONLY
# ============================================================
# READ THIS FIRST: this site does not use environment variables.
#
# It is a static site — plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript with no
# build step. Nothing compiles the code before the browser
# receives it, so there is no moment at which a variable like
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL could be substituted into the files.
# A .env file sitting in the folder would simply be ignored.
#
# The real settings live in JavaScript, and that is the correct
# pattern for a static Supabase site:
#
#   production-coordination/quiz/quiz-config.js   <- the quiz
#   app.js                                        <- the form
#   admin.js                                      <- the admin page
#
# This file exists so the two values are written down in one
# obvious place, and so you know where to look when someone
# hands you a checklist that asks for a .env.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT TO ADD IN VERCEL
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing. Deploy with framework preset "Other", build command
# blank, output directory ".". There are no environment
# variables to configure.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# ABOUT THE ANON KEY
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# The anon key is designed to be public — any key a browser uses
# is visible to anyone who presses F12. What protects the data is
# the Row Level Security policy, not secrecy. For this quiz the
# public key may INSERT an attempt and nothing else; it cannot
# read the table at all.
#
# NEVER put the service_role key in any file in this folder. That
# key ignores every security rule and belongs only on a server.
# ============================================================

# The Supabase project this site writes to.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# The "anon" / publishable key from
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# The service_role key is deliberately NOT listed here.
# It must never appear in a static site.
